    "notes": "Spec section 9 defines how to use this file. A trigger is a hint; nothing here tests what a consumer does after accepting one. input is the scanned, opened or pasted text and channel is scan, deeplink or paste. An accept lists via (url or legacy-json), from, id (null for legacy), exp (epoch seconds or null), flow (the config label, or null for an unhinted trigger), task (uri, major, minor, or null) and ignored (members not read, in document order: query._x for a reserved-prefix name this version does not define, legacy.x). Parameters whose names do not begin with an underscore are ignored and never reported. flows are matched by the whole Type URI minus its version segment, never by slug. config.skew is the clock-skew allowance in seconds: a trigger is expired when exp + skew <= now. The authority wallet.asml.berkmancenter.org is a provisional private identifier and tasks.example.org and the flow example-stable are test-only. ui is derived from reason: update = unknown-flow, unsupported-version; expired = expired; scan-only = wrong-channel; pass-on = not-ours; invalid = every other reason; unreachable is a selection outcome. selectionVectors has its own shape (a DID document in, a selection outcome out) and tests spec section 6 rule 5 only; each service endpoint is judged by the host rules of spec section 6 rule 6. Reasons and ui are as for the other vectors.",
